# PowerShell static-analysis scope for xp-gate Gate 1 (PSScriptAnalyzer).
#
# One path per line: a directory or a single file. Blank lines and lines that
# start with '#' are ignored. Every listed path must exist — a missing entry is
# reported fail-closed, which is the point: it means product code escaped the
# declared scope.
#
# Why this file exists at all
# ---------------------------
# xp-gate #595. Without it, adapters/powershell.sh takes its legacy branch and
# runs `Invoke-ScriptAnalyzer -Path . -Recurse`, which walks *the entire repo
# including node_modules*. Playwright ships three .ps1 helper scripts there
# (install_webkit_wsl.ps1, reinstall_chrome_beta_win.ps1, install_media_pack.ps1)
# that use Write-Host and a WMI cmdlet, so every commit was blocked by findings
# in third-party code that cannot be edited and is overwritten by `npm ci`.
#
# Note the same adapter's own _find_ps_files helper already prunes node_modules —
# only the legacy branch skips that pruning. Declaring the scope explicitly opts
# into the scoped branch and keeps the gate judging our code only.
#
# Keep this list to the directories that actually hold our PowerShell. Adding a
# path here widens what the gate inspects; it does not silence findings.
scripts/
